>As of Oct 12, October to November came in under 90% of normal in 41 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, more often than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair ran 45% of normal on the middle of the grids, and March to April 2026 sits at 35%. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 15490 at 53%. On grid 16092 the preliminary estimate for July to August 2026 is 57.0.</p>"}
